        {
         "id": "q9",
         "value": "Invariant that keeps it aligned:<br/>a frame slot is re-armed <b>at the frame boundary</b>.<br/>QVGA luma-only / QQVGA &#8594; slot == one sensor frame &#8594; self-aligning (verified).<br/>Any <b>crop</b> &#8594; slot &lt; sensor frame &#8594; software re-arm must hit the boundary exactly (unreliable in Renode).",
         "style": "rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=11;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;",
         "parent": "b4",
         "vertex": "1",
         "geometry": {
          "x": 20,
          "y": 150,
          "width": 760,
          "height": 90
         }
        },
        {
         "id": "q10",
         "value": "Timing budget @ 320x240, VIDEO_FPS=24:<br/>period 41.7 ms &#183; SPI 22.5 MHz (/4) &#8594; ~29 ms of 81.4 KB SPI traffic<br/>pacer = 1000/VIDEO_FPS ms deadline, overruns drop debt instead of cascading<br/>measured 24.00 fps emulated; host-observed ~0.1 fps is Renode throughput, not firmware<br/>host-observed rate &#8800; emulated rate &#8212; always report the emulated one.",
         "style": "rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=11;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;",
         "parent": "b4",
