          "y": 150,
          "width": 700,
          "height": 90
         }
        },
        {
         "id": "q11",
         "value": "Buffer arithmetic (why QVGA YUV422 is impossible):<br/>YUV422 = 2 byte/pixel &#8594; 320x240 = 153,600 B &gt; 128 KB RAM (fails at link: <i>region RAM overflowed</i>)<br/>luma-only via DCMI byte select = 1 byte/pixel &#8594; 76,800 B &#8594; fits<br/>QQVGA 160x120 YUV422 = 38,400 B/frame &#8594; 2-frame ring = 76,800 B &#8594; verified<br/>OV7670 has no YUV420; F4 DCMI has no CGR/CCMR &#8594; chroma must be stripped on the CPU.",
         "style": "rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=11;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;",
